<https://members-api.parliament.uk/api/Members/5053> <http://schema.org/sameAs> <https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&#038;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2F104031649007599_985128787556954&#038;title=%09On%20Workers%E2%80%99%20Memorial%20Day%2C%20I%E2%80%99m%20thinking%20back%20to%20last%20September%2C%20when%20I%20had%20the%20privilege%20of%20attending%20the%2075th%20memorial%20service%20for%20the%20Creswell%20Colliery%20disaster%20at%20St%20Mary%20Magdalene%20Church.It%20was%20a%20truly%20moving%20service.%20One%20gentleman%20told%20me%20how%20his%20father%20had%20swapped%20shifts%20with%20a%20man%20who%20was%20tragically%20killed%20that%20day.%20Another%20spoke%20about%20losing%20his%20father%20as%20a%20baby%20and%20growing%20up%20without%20ever%20knowing%20him.And%20then%20there%20are%20those%20who%20still%20carry%20the%20loss%20of%20friends%20and%20colleagues%20all%20these%20years%20on%2C%20a%20reminder%20of%20just%20how%20far-reaching%20the%20impact%20of%20workplace%20tragedy%20can%20be.Today%20is%20about%20remembering%20them%20and%20renewing%20our%20commitment%20to%20making%20sure%20every%20worker%20is%20safe%2C%20protected%2C%20and%20able%20to%20come%20home%20to%20their%20loved%20ones.%20%09%09> <https://forgetmenot.local/graph/identity/scraped> .
